From 8445cb0bb0f669b3ec8462a871339d154e34821e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Port <port@local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:04:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/25] drm/msm/dpu: add Khaje 6.10 catalog

Add an independent Khaje catalog from the Topaz FDT and Creek Khaje
revision data. Keep a dedicated compatible; do not alias SM6375 or
SM6115. The catalog exposes only upstream-representable features and
uses Topaz-derived offsets, QoS, bandwidth, CDP, VBIF remap and memtypes.

Add the Khaje VBIF shareability operation as a per-XIN read/modify/write.
The Creek implementation computes a masked value but writes zero to the
whole register; this port avoids reproducing that apparent vendor bug.

This does not reparent or enable the Topaz DT nodes, add DT bindings, or
claim Smart DMA v2.5, per-pipe priorities, advanced DSPP, QSYNC, secure-UI,
or full SDE feature parity. Hardware IRQ and resource integration remain
unvalidated.
